2026-08-12T11:50:44.612830Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019ff5cb-4a37-7b72-9194-6436615e7fb6" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420 turn.id=019ff5cb-4a37-7b72-9194-6436615e7fb6 model=gpt-5.6-sol codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: specs/005-referral-program/research.md\n@@\n-**Decision**: Use the singleton row as the database serialization point. Referral relationship/entitlement creation and recovery claim acquisition take a shared lock on the enabled row within their transaction. The operational update takes an exclusive lock, changes `enabled/revision`, and returns only after earlier shared-lock holders complete. Delivery rechecks the authoritative state immediately before the wallet command; claimed work is returned to retryable pending state when disabled.\n+**Decision**: Use the singleton row as the database serialization point. Referral relationship/entitlement creation and recovery claim acquisition take a shared lock on the enabled row within their transaction. Add a narrow trusted wallet method for referral credit that takes the same shared row lock inside the wallet ledger transaction immediately before the idempotent ledger insert. The operational update takes an exclusive lock, changes `enabled/revision`, and returns only after earlier shared-lock holders complete. Claimed work is returned to retryable pending state when disabled.\n@@\n-**Rationale**: This gives precise semantics across API instances without a distributed cache. The existing wallet call is idempotent but occurs in its own transaction, so a pre-delivery recheck is also required. Tests must pause at lock/check hooks to prove both orderings.\n+**Rationale**: This gives precise semantics across API instances without a distributed cache. A service-layer precheck alone is insufficient because the existing wallet credit uses its own transaction. The wallet remains the sole ledger writer; the new trusted method only adds the feature-state guard. Tests must pause at lock/check hooks to prove both orderings.\n@@\n-**Alternatives considered**: A bounded cache cannot give the required post-toggle boundary. Holding a database transaction open across arbitrary network I/O was rejected; the wallet boundary is currently local PostgreSQL but should remain independently idempotent. Cancelling historical obligations was rejected.\n+**Alternatives considered**: A bounded cache or service-layer recheck cannot give the required post-toggle boundary. Holding a database transaction open across arbitrary network I/O was rejected. Cancelling historical obligations was rejected.\n@@\n-**Decision**: Drop the `ReferralEligibility` table and its user relation in the new migration after code no longer reads it. It is transient permission state, not an accounting fact, and is no longer meaningful. Do not cascade to users, relationships, entitlements, or wallet rows.\n+**Decision**: Use two migrations. The expand migration adds/seeds the feature-state row and leaves `ReferralEligibility` available for rolling compatibility. After all old API instances are drained and the new backend no longer reads or writes eligibility, a contract migration drops the `ReferralEligibility` table and its user relation. It is transient permission state, not an accounting fact, and is no longer meaningful. Do not cascade to users, relationships, entitlements, or wallet rows.\n*** End Patch";
text(await tools.apply_patch(patch));
