2026-08-12T12:11:44.170171Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019ff5de-ba59-7221-a032-3894fc082522" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420 turn.id=019ff5de-ba59-7221-a032-3894fc082522 model=gpt-5.6-sol codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Delete File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/005-referral-program/tasks.md\n*** Add File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/005-referral-program/tasks.md\n+# Tasks: Referral Program Scope Revision\n+\n+**Input**: Design documents from `specs/005-referral-program/`\n+\n+**Prerequisites**: `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `research.md`, `data-model.md`,\n+`contracts/`, and `quickstart.md`\n+\n+**Tests**: Required by the specification and quickstart. Story test tasks are\n+listed before implementation tasks and must initially fail for the revised\n+behavior.\n+\n+**Migration context**: The referral feature already exists. These tasks migrate\n+the current implementation; they do not recreate it. Historical relationships,\n+entitlements, wallet operations, and promo codes are preserved.\n+\n+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story?] Description`\n+\n+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel because it targets different files and has no\n+  dependency on another incomplete task in the same phase.\n+- **[US#]**: Maps the task to a user story in `spec.md`.\n+- Every task names the exact file or files it changes.\n+\n+## Technical Phase Mapping\n+\n+| Requested technical work | Task phase |\n+|---|---|\n+| Additive migration and persistent feature state | Phases 1-2 |\n+| Registration-only inviter bonus | Phase 3, US1 |\n+| Remove welcome/apply/eligibility behavior | Phase 3, US1 |\n+| Operational API, curl, and package commands | Phase 4, US2 |\n+| Public availability and `FEATURE_DISABLED` | Phase 4, US2 |\n+| Recovery pause/resume and wallet race barrier | Phase 4, US2 |\n+| Mobile MobX/RxJS availability and hidden UI | Phase 5, US3 |\n+| Eligibility contract migration | Phase 7 |\n+| Contract, integration, concurrency, mobile, and rollout validation | Phase 8 |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 1: Setup - Additive Migration And Configuration\n+\n+**Purpose**: Introduce the durable flag without changing current enabled\n+behavior or historical referral data.\n+\n+- [ ] T001 Add the singleton `ReferralFeatureState` Prisma model and the enabled-by-default, idempotent seed migration in `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma` and `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260812000100_add_referral_feature_state/migration.sql`\n+- [ ] T002 Add PostgreSQL migration assertions for seeded enabled state, constraints, restart persistence, and unchanged referral/wallet row counts in `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T003 [P] Replace `REFERRAL_WELCOME_BONUS_ML` with validated `REFERRAL_OPERATIONS_TOKEN` configuration while retaining `REFERRAL_INVITER_BONUS_ML` in `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`, `apps/api/src/config/env.referral.spec.ts`, and `apps/api/.env.example`\n+- [ ] T004 [P] Add fixture helpers for reading, resetting, and locking the singleton feature row through independent Prisma clients in `apps/api/test/referral-postgres.fixture.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: The expand migration is deployable first, seeds existing\n+installations as enabled, and does not alter accounting facts.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 2: Foundational - Persistent Feature State Boundary\n+\n+**Purpose**: Provide one server-authoritative availability boundary shared by\n+registration, public reads, operations, recovery, and the wallet guard.\n+\n+**CRITICAL**: Complete this phase before any user-story implementation.\n+\n+- [ ] T005 Define typed read, shared-lock assertion, and idempotent exclusive-update ports for `REFERRAL_PROGRAM` in `apps/api/src/referral/application/ports/referral-feature-state.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T006 [P] Add service unit tests for enabled/disabled reads, same-value updates, revision transitions, and fail-closed storage errors in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-feature-state.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T007 [P] Add PostgreSQL tests using independent Prisma clients for shared/exclusive lock ordering, idempotent updates, revision monotonicity, and multi-instance visibility in `apps/api/test/referral-feature-state.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T008 Implement the feature-state application service without an authoritative in-memory cache in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-feature-state.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T009 Implement the Prisma repository and transactional lock operations in `apps/api/src/referral/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-referral-feature-state.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T010 Register the feature-state port, repository, and service for shared use in `apps/api/src/referral/referral.module.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: All API instances obtain availability from the same persistent\n+row, and storage failure cannot silently enable referral effects.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Apply A Promo Code During Registration (Priority: P1) MVP\n+\n+**Goal**: Complete registration with optional pending promo context, creating\n+one relationship and one inviter bonus only for a valid code while enabled.\n+Remove welcome, invitee, post-registration apply, and purchase-eligibility\n+behavior from the active implementation.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Complete no-code, valid, invalid, unavailable, and self\n+registrations after OTP and legal acceptance; replace/remove pending context;\n+retry and race completion; verify only the valid enabled case creates one\n+`REGISTRATION` relationship, one `INVITER` entitlement, and one inviter wallet\n+credit, with no invitee or welcome credit.\n+\n+### Tests For User Story 1\n+\n+- [ ] T011 [P] [US1] Rewrite onboarding unit tests for no-code, valid, invalid, self, disabled, welcome-free, and invitee-credit-free outcomes in `apps/api/src/auth/application/registration.service.spec.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-provisioning.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T012 [P] [US1] Rewrite PostgreSQL registration acceptance tests for OTP/legal ordering, final pending-code selection, one inviter entitlement, and zero registering-user referral operations in `apps/api/test/referral-registration.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T013 [P] [US1] Add replay and competing-code completion tests proving one immutable inviter relationship and one inviter credit in `apps/api/test/referral-concurrency.integration-spec.ts` and `apps/api/src/auth/application/registration-concurrency.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T014 [P] [US1] Update registration HTTP contract tests to preserve auth/session responses while removing post-registration referral application behavior in `apps/api/test/registration-http.contract-spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-http.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T015 [P] [US1] Rewrite delivery tests so only `INVITER` entitlements can reach the wallet and legacy `WELCOME` rows remain inert in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-bonus-delivery.service.spec.ts`\n+\n+### Implementation For User Story 1\n+\n+- [ ] T016 [US1] Replace the onboarding boundary with registration-completion input/result semantics and remove post-registration command types in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-registration.integration.ts`\n+- [ ] T017 [US1] Refactor the Prisma registration integration to lock availability in the registration transaction, provision a stable user code, and atomically create only `REGISTRATION`/`INVITER` facts in `apps/api/src/referral/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-referral-registration.integration.ts`\n+- [ ] T018 [US1] Invoke referral completion only after OTP, current legal acceptance, and successful registration finalization while consuming the final pending promo context in `apps/api/src/auth/application/registration.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T019 [US1] Restrict provisioning to idempotent stable promo-code creation and remove eligibility creation in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-provisioning.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/infrastructure/postgres/referral-promo-provisioner.ts`\n+- [ ] T020 [US1] Remove welcome/invitee entitlement creation and post-registration application methods from `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-application.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T021 [US1] Restrict delivery constants and logic to inviter obligations without modifying historical delivered wallet operations in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-bonus-delivery.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/domain/referral-types.ts`\n+- [ ] T022 [US1] Remove eligibility, welcome, post-registration application, and attached-code operations from the repository port and Prisma repository while retaining historical enum/channel reads in `apps/api/src/referral/application/ports/referral.repository.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-referral.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T023 [US1] Delete the active eligibility service and purchase-close boundary files `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-eligibility.service.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-eligibility.service.spec.ts`, and `apps/api/src/referral/composition/close-referral-eligibility.ts`\n+- [ ] T024 [US1] Remove application request DTOs, eligibility/attached-code response fields, and stale application error mappings in `apps/api/src/referral/http/dto/referral-request.dto.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/http/dto/referral-response.dto.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-response.mapper.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-response.mapper.spec.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-error.filter.ts`, and `apps/api/src/referral/domain/referral-errors.ts`\n+- [ ] T025 [US1] Remove `POST /v1/referrals/applications` and its injected application service from `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral.controller.ts`\n+- [ ] T026 [US1] Remove eligibility/application providers and purchase-close exports while retaining registration, query, recovery, and provisioning composition in `apps/api/src/referral/referral.module.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/referral.module.spec.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US1 is independently usable as the MVP. Registration is the\n+only referral-application point and never rewards the registering user.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Control Referral Availability (Priority: P1)\n+\n+**Goal**: Let authorized operators toggle a persistent runtime flag through\n+HTTP, curl, and root package commands; enforce the state across public APIs,\n+registration, recovery, and the final wallet-write boundary.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Toggle through curl and package commands, repeat each\n+operation, reject bad credentials/body, restart and use multiple API instances,\n+register while disabled, and pause/resume a pending inviter entitlement without\n+creating a duplicate credit.\n+\n+### Operational API, Curl, And Package Commands\n+\n+- [ ] T027 [P] [US2] Add strict operational GET/PUT contract tests for authentication, validation, no-store headers, idempotent revision behavior, and secret-safe failures in `apps/api/test/referral-feature-operations.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T028 [P] [US2] Add unit tests for constant-time bearer-token validation and strict boolean-only DTO input in `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-operations.guard.spec.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/http/dto/referral-feature-operation.dto.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T029 [US2] Implement the dedicated operations bearer guard without logging or returning credentials in `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-operations.guard.ts`\n+- [ ] T030 [P] [US2] Implement strict operational request/response DTO shaping with decimal-string revisions in `apps/api/src/referral/http/dto/referral-feature-operation.dto.ts`\n+- [ ] T031 [US2] Implement protected, no-store `GET` and idempotent `PUT /internal/feature-flags/referral-program` outside public Swagger in `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-feature-operations.controller.ts`\n+- [ ] T032 [US2] Register the operational controller and guard in `apps/api/src/referral/referral.module.ts`\n+- [ ] T033 [P] [US2] Add Node tests for missing env, enable/disable, PUT-then-GET verification, malformed/non-2xx responses, state mismatch, network failure, and token redaction in `scripts/set-referral-feature.test.mjs`\n+- [ ] T034 [US2] Implement the environment-driven HTTP helper with strict failure handling and authoritative read-back in `scripts/set-referral-feature.mjs`\n+- [ ] T035 [US2] Add root `referral:enable` and `referral:disable` scripts that pass no repository secret in `package.json`\n+\n+### Public Availability And `FEATURE_DISABLED`\n+\n+- [ ] T036 [P] [US2] Add public app-config contract tests for exact privacy-safe shape, no-store headers, storage failure, and live multi-instance changes in `apps/api/test/app-config.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T037 [P] [US2] Add referral HTTP tests requiring identical `503 FEATURE_DISABLED` envelopes from both public referral reads while registration remains available in `apps/api/test/referral-http.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T038 [US2] Implement the public app-config response DTO and unauthenticated no-store controller in `apps/api/src/app-config/http/dto/app-config-response.dto.ts` and `apps/api/src/app-config/http/app-config.controller.ts`\n+- [ ] T039 [US2] Compose the public app-config endpoint with the referral availability service in `apps/api/src/app-config/app-config.module.ts` and `apps/api/src/app.module.ts`\n+- [ ] T040 [US2] Add stable `FEATURE_DISABLED` domain-to-HTTP mapping without exposing preserved data in `apps/api/src/referral/domain/referral-errors.ts`, `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral-error.filter.ts`, and `apps/api/src/referral/http/referral.controller.ts`\n+- [ ] T041 [US2] Gate referral summary and invitation queries with an authoritative availability read in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-query.service.ts`\n+\n+### Recovery Pause/Resume And Wallet Race Barrier\n+\n+- [ ] T042 [P] [US2] Rewrite recovery unit tests for inviter-only claims, disabled zero-claim behavior, lost-guard release, legacy welcome exclusion, and re-enabled idempotent delivery in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-recovery.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T043 [P] [US2] Add PostgreSQL race tests for toggle-before-claim, toggle-after-claim, wallet-commit/link failure, concurrent workers, and both toggle/registration lock orders in `apps/api/test/referral-recovery.integration-spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-concurrency.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T044 [US2] Extend the trusted wallet command boundary with referral feature-guard context in `apps/api/src/wallet/application/wallet-command.ts` and `apps/api/src/wallet/application/ports/wallet.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T045 [US2] Acquire the shared feature-row lock immediately before the idempotent referral ledger insert in `apps/api/src/wallet/application/wallet-command.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/wallet/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-wallet.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T046 [US2] Pause inviter claims while disabled and safely release or resume already claimed obligations in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-recovery.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/composition/referral-recovery.scheduler.ts`\n+- [ ] T047 [US2] Pass the trusted feature guard through live delivery and recovery CLI composition in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-bonus-delivery.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/cli/recover-referral-bonuses.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US2 is independently testable through both operator interfaces;\n+after a successful disable boundary, no new relationship, entitlement, or\n+referral wallet credit can start, and pending inviter work resumes once.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Share My Referral Code (Priority: P2)\n+\n+**Goal**: Preserve enabled code/link sharing while making server availability\n+the MobX-owned source for registration and referral UI, with RxJS cancellation\n+and complete removal of signed-in apply behavior.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Load enabled availability, view/copy/share a stable code,\n+open a link while signed out and signed in, disable during active requests and\n+registration, then verify all referral UI/context is hidden or cleared and late\n+results cannot restore it.\n+\n+### Tests For User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T048 [P] [US3] Add cold Observable app-config adapter tests for strict response shaping, abort teardown, and privacy-field rejection in `apps/mobile/src/api/app-config-api.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T049 [P] [US3] Add MobX tests for unknown/loading/enabled/disabled/error transitions, revision-free public state, and atomic clearing on session replacement in `apps/mobile/src/features/stores/feature-availability.store.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T050 [P] [US3] Add RxJS service tests for refresh, stale-request cancellation, disable publication, session replacement, retry, and disposal in `apps/mobile/src/features/services/feature-availability.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T051 [P] [US3] Rewrite mobile referral API/store/flow tests to remove apply and eligibility state and reject stale data after disable in `apps/mobile/src/api/referral-api.spec.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/referral/stores/referral.store.spec.ts`, and `apps/mobile/src/referral/services/referral-flow.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T052 [P] [US3] Rewrite deep-link tests for enabled anonymous pending context, disabled/unknown rejection, and unconditional signed-in ignore behavior in `apps/mobile/src/navigation/referral-link-coordinator.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T053 [P] [US3] Update auth/navigation UI tests for hidden promo input/routes, disable-during-registration clearing, enabled sharing, and logout/session isolation in `apps/mobile/__tests__/phone-auth-flow.test.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/navigation/AuthNavigator.spec.ts`, and `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.spec.tsx`\n+\n+### Implementation For User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T054 [US3] Implement a typed cold Observable public app-config adapter with AbortController teardown in `apps/mobile/src/api/app-config-api.ts`\n+- [ ] T055 [US3] Implement `FeatureAvailabilityStore` as the sole owner of unknown/loading/enabled/disabled/error availability state in `apps/mobile/src/features/stores/feature-availability.store.ts`\n+- [ ] T056 [US3] Implement the disposable RxJS refresh/cancellation workflow that publishes authoritative availability to MobX in `apps/mobile/src/features/services/feature-availability.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T057 [US3] Compose and dispose app-config availability with auth and referral scopes in `apps/mobile/src/App.tsx` and `apps/mobile/src/auth/auth-composition-root.ts`\n+- [ ] T058 [US3] Remove apply operations and eligibility/attached-code state while invalidating in-flight reads on disable or session epoch change in `apps/mobile/src/api/referral-api.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/referral/stores/referral.store.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/referral/services/referral-flow.service.ts`, and `apps/mobile/src/referral/referral-composition-root.ts`\n+- [ ] T059 [US3] Make anonymous deep links populate editable pending context only while enabled and ignore all signed-in referral links in `apps/mobile/src/navigation/referral-link-coordinator.ts`\n+- [ ] T060 [US3] Hide or clear registration promo context while availability is unknown/disabled and omit it from completion payloads in `apps/mobile/src/auth/stores/registration.store.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/auth/services/registration-flow.service.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/auth/services/otp-flow.service.ts`, and `apps/mobile/src/auth/screens/PhoneEntryScreen.tsx`\n+- [ ] T061 [US3] Delete `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ApplyReferralCodeScreen.tsx` and `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ApplyReferralCodeScreen.spec.tsx`, then remove the route, imports, callbacks, and signed-in navigation binding from `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.tsx`\n+- [ ] T062 [US3] Observe availability in root/main navigation, hide referral entry points and routes while unknown/disabled, and leave an active referral route on disable in `apps/mobile/src/navigation/RootNavigator.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.tsx`, and `apps/mobile/src/wallet/screens/WalletScreen.tsx`\n+- [ ] T063 [US3] Preserve enabled code/link rendering and copy/share actions without apply controls in `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ReferralScreen.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ReferralScreen.spec.tsx`, and `apps/mobile/src/referral/native/referral-native-actions.spec.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US3 remains independently testable when enabled, while disabled\n+and unknown states expose no referral navigation, content, input, or retained\n+deep-link context.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Review Referral Results (Priority: P2)\n+\n+**Goal**: Preserve privacy-safe inviter totals and deterministic paginated\n+history while enabled, and return no data while disabled.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Load zero, one-page, and multi-page histories for separate\n+inviters, verify exact credited inviter-only totals and stable ordering, then\n+disable and re-enable without changing or duplicating stored data.\n+\n+### Tests For User Story 4\n+\n+- [ ] T064 [P] [US4] Update query unit tests for inviter-only credited totals, privacy-safe rows, stable pagination, owner isolation, and enabled-state enforcement in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-query.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T065 [P] [US4] Update PostgreSQL repository tests for preserved history, deterministic cursors, inviter-only totals, and unchanged data across toggles in `apps/api/test/referral-repository.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T066 [P] [US4] Update mobile history tests for zero, loaded, pagination, retry, disable clearing, re-enable reload, and stale page rejection in `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ReferralScreen.spec.tsx`\n+\n+### Implementation For User Story 4\n+\n+- [ ] T067 [US4] Remove eligibility/application fields from referral summary projection while retaining owner-scoped inviter totals and privacy-safe cursor history in `apps/api/src/referral/application/referral-query.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/referral/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-referral.repository.ts`\n+- [ ] T068 [US4] Keep summary/history MobX and RxJS pagination state enabled-only, serialized, session-scoped, and resettable on disable in `apps/mobile/src/referral/stores/referral.store.ts` and `apps/mobile/src/referral/services/referral-flow.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T069 [US4] Render zero/loaded/paginated inviter history from API truth and suppress all content/actions when unavailable in `apps/mobile/src/referral/screens/ReferralScreen.tsx`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US4 reports only credited inviter outcomes, remains private and\n+deterministic, and preserves data invisibly through a disabled interval.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 7: Eligibility Contract Migration\n+\n+**Purpose**: Remove transient purchase-eligibility storage only after all new\n+runtime code is deployed and old API instances have been drained.\n+\n+- [ ] T070 Prove no runtime code or generated client references `ReferralEligibility` before contraction in `apps/api/src/referral/referral-boundaries.spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T071 Add a non-cascading contract migration that drops only `ReferralEligibility` constraints/table and remove its Prisma relation/model while retaining legacy bonus/channel enum values in `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260812000200_drop_referral_eligibility/migration.sql` and `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`\n+- [ ] T072 Add contract-migration acceptance assertions for preserved users, promo codes, relationships, entitlements, and wallet ledger rows plus rollback rehearsal expectations in `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: Eligibility storage is absent only after the rolling-deployment\n+drain gate, with no cascade or rewrite of historical accounting data.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 8: Contracts, Integration, Concurrency, Mobile, And Rollout Validation\n+\n+**Purpose**: Synchronize source/generated contracts and close all cross-story,\n+security, concurrency, visual, migration, rollout, and rollback gates.\n+\n+- [ ] T073 Remove the post-registration operation and eligibility schemas, add public app-config and `FEATURE_DISABLED`, and keep internal operations out of public Swagger in `specs/005-referral-program/contracts/openapi.yaml`\n+- [ ] T074 [P] Verify the protected GET/PUT implementation remains aligned with its standalone internal contract in `specs/005-referral-program/contracts/operational-feature-flag.openapi.yaml` and `apps/api/test/referral-feature-operations.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T075 Regenerate the aggregate public artifact after updating generator inputs in `apps/api/src/openapi/generate-openapi.ts` and `specs/005-referral-program/contracts/openapi.generated.json`\n+- [ ] T076 Add aggregate contract assertions for app-config, disabled errors, removed apply route/schemas, and exclusion of operational routes in `apps/api/test/openapi.contract-spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-http.contract-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T077 [P] Add static regression checks that welcome env/config, public apply route, eligibility-close command, apply screen, and active eligibility access cannot return in `apps/api/src/referral/referral-boundaries.spec.ts`, `apps/api/src/config/env.referral.spec.ts`, and `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T078 Run and record the quickstart curl/package-script scenarios, unauthorized/failed toggles, restart persistence, three-instance consistency, enabled/disabled registration, preserved data, and exactly-once recovery in `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/runtime-rollout-validation.md`\n+- [ ] T079 Run and record targeted API typecheck, unit, OpenAPI, PostgreSQL migration, registration, recovery, wallet-race, and concurrency results in `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/backend-validation.md`\n+- [ ] T080 Run and record mobile typecheck/build/tests plus iOS and Android comparison with `docs/design/mockups/06_referral_program_hd.png` for enabled hierarchy and disabled UI absence in `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/mobile-visual.md`\n+- [ ] T081 Document the executed rollout order, old-instance drain evidence, historical row-count checks, disabled-first rollback procedure, and residual risks in `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/rollout-readiness.md`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies & Execution Order\n+\n+### Phase Dependencies\n+\n+- **Phase 1 - Setup**: Starts immediately; the additive migration must deploy\n+  before backend code expects the feature row.\n+- **Phase 2 - Foundational**: Depends on Phase 1 and blocks all user stories.\n+- **Phase 3 - US1**: Depends on Phase 2; establishes the revised registration\n+  and inviter-only domain behavior.\n+- **Phase 4 - US2**: Depends on Phase 2 and uses the US1 registration boundary\n+  for disabled/toggle race validation. Finish US1 before the final US2 race\n+  tasks T043-T047.\n+- **Phase 5 - US3**: Depends on Phase 4 public app-config availability; enabled\n+  sharing can otherwise be developed independently from US4 history work.\n+- **Phase 6 - US4**: Depends on Phase 4 server gating and Phase 5 shared mobile\n+  availability/store lifecycle.\n+- **Phase 7 - Contract Migration**: Depends on Phases 3-6 and may run only after\n+  all old API instances are drained.\n+- **Phase 8 - Validation**: Depends on every selected story and the migration\n+  phase intended for that rollout.\n+\n+### User Story Dependencies\n+\n+- **US1 (P1)**: Begins after the persistent flag foundation; no dependency on\n+  sharing or history UI.\n+- **US2 (P1)**: Begins after the persistent flag foundation; operational API\n+  and public availability are independently testable before recovery race tests\n+  integrate with US1.\n+- **US3 (P2)**: Requires the US2 public availability contract, but not US4.\n+- **US4 (P2)**: Requires the shared US2 gating and US3 availability lifecycle;\n+  backend query tests can begin after Phase 2.\n+\n+### Within Each User Story\n+\n+- Write the listed story tests first and confirm revised assertions fail.\n+- Implement boundary models/ports before services and controllers.\n+- Implement server availability before mobile consumption.\n+- Run focused unit/contract tests before PostgreSQL race suites.\n+- Do not apply the eligibility contract migration until runtime references are\n+  absent and old binaries are drained.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Parallel Opportunities\n+\n+### User Story 1\n+\n+```text\n+T011: registration/provisioning unit tests\n+T012: PostgreSQL registration acceptance tests\n+T013: replay and competing-code concurrency tests\n+T014: registration/referral HTTP contract tests\n+T015: inviter-only delivery unit tests\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 2\n+\n+```text\n+T027: operational HTTP contract tests\n+T028: operational guard/DTO unit tests\n+T033: root helper Node tests\n+T036: public app-config contract tests\n+T037: FEATURE_DISABLED referral HTTP tests\n+T042: recovery unit tests\n+T043: PostgreSQL race tests after US1 registration semantics are complete\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 3\n+\n+```text\n+T048: app-config adapter tests\n+T049: MobX availability-store tests\n+T050: RxJS availability-service tests\n+T051: referral API/store/flow migration tests\n+T052: deep-link tests\n+T053: auth/navigation UI tests\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 4\n+\n+```text\n+T064: query-service tests\n+T065: PostgreSQL repository tests\n+T066: mobile history tests\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Strategy\n+\n+### MVP First\n+\n+1. Complete Phases 1 and 2.\n+2. Complete Phase 3 (US1).\n+3. Validate registration independently, including absence of invitee/welcome\n+   credit and idempotent inviter-only delivery.\n+4. Do not ship the revised behavior without the US2 kill switch if runtime\n+   disablement is part of the release acceptance gate.\n+\n+### Incremental Delivery\n+\n+1. Deploy the additive feature-state migration seeded enabled.\n+2. Deploy US1 and US2 backend code, then verify operational disable/enable,\n+   public availability, registration gating, and recovery barriers.\n+3. Release US3/US4 mobile behavior after the server app-config contract exists.\n+4. Drain every old backend instance and only then apply the eligibility contract\n+   migration.\n+5. Complete Phase 8 evidence before enabling referral acquisition after rollout.\n+\n+### Rollback Rule\n+\n+Disable referrals first, then roll back only to a schema-compatible binary that\n+cannot recreate welcome or post-registration behavior. Never reverse wallet\n+credits, delete historical referral facts, or use a destructive data down\n+migration.\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+- `[P]` tasks target different files or independent test fixtures.\n+- Story labels provide traceability to `spec.md`; setup, foundational,\n+  migration, and final validation tasks intentionally have no story label.\n+- Legacy `WELCOME` and `POST_REGISTRATION` enum values remain historical-only;\n+  retaining them is not permission to create new rows.\n+- `ReferralEligibility` remains only for rolling compatibility until Phase 7.\n+- Commit and validate one logical diff at a time in the listed dependency order.\n*** End Patch";
text(await tools.apply_patch(patch));
