2026-08-13T09:22:23.047809Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019ffa65-96a9-7da0-ae41-ddee83667926" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019ff5ad-b076-7e13-9fc1-4c2a2ad98420 turn.id=019ffa65-96a9-7da0-ae41-ddee83667926 model=gpt-5.6-sol codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/005-referral-program/checklists/rollout-readiness.md\n+# Referral Eligibility Contract Rollout Readiness\n+\n+## Prepared Evidence\n+\n+| Gate | Status | Evidence |\n+|------|--------|----------|\n+| T070 runtime boundary | PASS | `referral-boundaries.spec.ts`: production referral code has no `ReferralEligibility` or `referralEligibility` reference |\n+| T070 generated client boundary | PASS | Contract acceptance confirms the generated `PrismaClient` has no `referralEligibility` delegate |\n+| T071 contract migration | PREPARED ONLY | `20260812000200_drop_referral_eligibility` uses explicit `DROP TABLE`, `DROP FUNCTION`, and `DROP TYPE` statements without `CASCADE` |\n+| T072 disposable migration | PASS | 2026-08-13: `referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`, 11 tests passed against local disposable PostgreSQL schemas |\n+| T072 compatible binary | PASS | Prisma generation and API typecheck pass against the contracted schema; preserved models remain queryable after migration |\n+\n+The disposable acceptance seed includes users, a promo code, a relationship, an\n+inviter entitlement, a wallet, a wallet ledger row, and a legacy eligibility\n+row. The post-migration assertions compare preserved row counts and retrieve the\n+historical relationship and entitlement through the newly generated client.\n+\n+## Blocking T073 Application Gate\n+\n+Status: **NOT EXECUTED**\n+\n+The contract migration must not be applied to a shared environment until every\n+field below is recorded and approved immediately before application.\n+\n+| Required evidence | Recorded value |\n+|-------------------|----------------|\n+| Target environment | Pending |\n+| Compatible deployed API version(s) | Pending |\n+| Proof each live version passed the T070 boundary | Pending |\n+| Old-instance termination/drain evidence | Pending |\n+| Responsible approver and timestamp | Pending |\n+| Migration application timestamp | Pending |\n+| Applied migration identity from `_prisma_migrations` | Pending |\n+| Pre/post user row count | Pending |\n+| Pre/post promo-code row count | Pending |\n+| Pre/post relationship row count | Pending |\n+| Pre/post entitlement row count | Pending |\n+| Pre/post wallet-ledger row count | Pending |\n+| Eligibility table/type/function absent | Pending |\n+| Referral availability and recovery health check | Pending |\n+\n+Any missing field blocks application. A local disposable migration run is not\n+approval for a shared environment.\n+\n+## Forward-Only Recovery\n+\n+After the contract migration, a legacy binary that references eligibility is\n+incompatible and must be rejected from deployment.\n+\n+1. Disable the referral feature through the authoritative operational endpoint.\n+2. Stop or replace the incompatible binary; do not recreate eligibility storage.\n+3. Deploy a corrected forward binary that is compatible with the contracted schema.\n+4. Do not run a down migration and do not synthesize deleted eligibility rows.\n+5. Verify preserved referral/accounting row counts and exactly-once recovery health.\n+6. Re-enable referral only after the corrected deployment and health checks pass.\n+\n+Rollback after contraction is therefore an application rollback only to a\n+known compatible build. Database recovery remains forward-only.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/005-referral-program/tasks.md\n@@\n-- [ ] T070 Prove no runtime code or generated client references `ReferralEligibility` before contraction in `apps/api/src/referral/referral-boundaries.spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`\n-- [ ] T071 Prepare the non-cascading contract migration that drops only `ReferralEligibility` constraints/table and remove its Prisma relation/model while retaining legacy bonus/channel enum values in `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260812000200_drop_referral_eligibility/migration.sql` and `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`; do not apply this migration to a shared environment yet\n-- [ ] T072 Add and run disposable-database contract-migration assertions for preserved users, promo codes, relationships, entitlements, and wallet ledger rows, prove the new binary works with the contracted schema, and document that post-contraction recovery rejects legacy binaries and uses a corrected forward deployment rather than a down migration or recreated eligibility data in `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts` and `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/rollout-readiness.md`\n+- [x] T070 Prove no runtime code or generated client references `ReferralEligibility` before contraction in `apps/api/src/referral/referral-boundaries.spec.ts` and `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [x] T071 Prepare the non-cascading contract migration that drops only `ReferralEligibility` constraints/table and remove its Prisma relation/model while retaining legacy bonus/channel enum values in `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260812000200_drop_referral_eligibility/migration.sql` and `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`; do not apply this migration to a shared environment yet\n+- [x] T072 Add and run disposable-database contract-migration assertions for preserved users, promo codes, relationships, entitlements, and wallet ledger rows, prove the new binary works with the contracted schema, and document that post-contraction recovery rejects legacy binaries and uses a corrected forward deployment rather than a down migration or recreated eligibility data in `apps/api/test/referral-migration.integration-spec.ts` and `specs/005-referral-program/checklists/rollout-readiness.md`\n*** End Patch";
text(await tools.apply_patch(patch));
