-    │   │   ├── MachineDiscoveryWorkflow.ts\n-    │   │   └── machineDiscovery.types.ts\n+    │   ├── stores/\n+    │   │   └── machine-discovery.store.ts\n+    │   ├── services/\n+    │   │   └── machine-discovery-flow.service.ts\n+    │   ├── machine-discovery.types.ts\n@@\n-    └── test/\n-        └── machine-discovery/\n+    └── testing/\n@@\n-- `machineId` is a cryptographically random, immutable, opaque 128-bit public\n+- `machineId` is a cryptographically random, immutable, opaque 128-bit public\n   identifier encoded as 22 base64url characters. It is distinct from the\n   internal UUID primary key and from customer-entered codes.\n+- A nullable catalog display name is mapped to a localized generic customer\n+  fallback; the fallback never embeds internal or public identifiers.\n@@\n-- Optional viewport bounds are validated, bounded, and cursor-bound. Invalid or\n-  missing machine coordinates are excluded from map/distance results but may be\n-  shown in list results without distance when their public address is valid.\n+- Optional viewport bounds are validated, bounded, and cursor-bound. Invalid or\n+  missing machine coordinates are excluded from map/distance results but may be\n+  shown in list results without distance when their public address and explicit\n+  application-owned service-area assignment are valid.\n@@\n-| `GET` | `/api/v1/machines` | Bounded incremental catalog discovery with optional location/viewport context |\n-| `GET` | `/api/v1/machines/{machineId}` | Fresh consumer-safe card/detail |\n-| `POST` | `/api/v1/machines/resolve` | Exact QR or manual-code resolution |\n-| `POST` | `/api/v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation` | Final current eligibility/price check and typed handoff |\n+| `GET` | `/v1/machines` | Bounded incremental catalog discovery with optional location/viewport context |\n+| `GET` | `/v1/machines/{machineId}` | Fresh consumer-safe card/detail |\n+| `POST` | `/v1/machines/resolve` | Exact QR or manual-code resolution |\n+| `POST` | `/v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation` | Final current eligibility/price check and typed handoff |\n*** Update File: specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/data-model.md\n@@\n-| `displayName` | VARCHAR(120) | Trimmed safe customer copy; no serial/modem/internal labels. |\n+| `displayName` | VARCHAR(120) nullable | Trimmed safe customer copy; null uses a localized generic fallback with no identifiers. |\n@@\n-- `machineId` is generated once and cannot be updated by repository methods.\n+- `machineId` is generated once; repository methods and a database trigger reject\n+  any update after insertion.\n+- The response mapper emits a localized equivalent of `Water machine` when\n+  `displayName` is null; it never appends internal UUID, public ID, alias, or\n+  serial/modem data.\n@@\n-| `machineInternalId` | UUID FK UNIQUE | Required owner; cascade delete only in non-production cleanup. |\n+| `machineInternalId` | UUID FK UNIQUE | Required owner; `ON DELETE RESTRICT`. |\n | `address` | VARCHAR(300) | Trimmed customer-safe display address. |\n+| `serviceAreaCode` | VARCHAR(64) | Explicit application-owned configured service-area assignment. |\n@@\n-- Missing/invalid coordinates exclude a machine from map markers and distance\n-  ranking. A published machine with a valid address may remain in unlocated list\n-  discovery with no `distanceMeters` field.\n+- Missing/invalid coordinates exclude a machine from map markers and distance\n+  ranking. A published machine with a valid address and configured\n+  `serviceAreaCode` may remain in unlocated list discovery with no\n+  `distanceMeters` field.\n@@\n-3. Checks for `machine_id` format, nonblank display/address, paired coordinates,\n-   coordinate ranges, positive decimal price, uppercase currency, and singleton\n-   catalog key.\n+3. Checks for `machine_id` format, nonblank optional display name/address,\n+   service-area code, paired coordinates, coordinate ranges, positive decimal\n+   price, uppercase currency, and singleton catalog key.\n@@\n-7. B-tree on valid coordinate pair for bounded prefiltering. Haversine remains a\n-   computed expression for MVP; inspect query plans before adding geospatial\n-   infrastructure.\n+7. B-tree on `service_area_code` and the valid coordinate pair for bounded\n+   rectangular prefiltering. Haversine remains a computed expression for MVP;\n+   inspect query plans before adding geospatial infrastructure.\n+8. Trigger rejecting any update to `machines.machine_id`.\n@@\n-3. Create location, price, identifier, evidence, and catalog-state tables with\n+3. Create location, price, identifier, evidence, and catalog-state tables with\n    foreign keys/check constraints.\n-4. Create unique, partial, and lookup indexes.\n-5. Insert the catalog singleton with revision `1`.\n-6. Do not insert machines, identifiers, prices, or evidence in the migration.\n+4. Create the public-identity immutability trigger.\n+5. Create unique, partial, and lookup indexes.\n+6. Insert the catalog singleton with revision `1`.\n+7. Do not insert machines, identifiers, prices, or evidence in the migration.\n*** Update File: specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/contracts/selection-handoff.md\n@@\n-  `POST /api/v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation`.\n+  `POST /v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation`.\n*** Update File: specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/contracts/machine-discovery.openapi.yaml\n@@\n-  /api/v1/machines:\n+  /v1/machines:\n@@\n-  /api/v1/machines/{machineId}:\n+  /v1/machines/{machineId}:\n@@\n-  /api/v1/machines/resolve:\n+  /v1/machines/resolve:\n@@\n-  /api/v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation:\n+  /v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation:\n*** End Patch";
