ion, version gating, repository lookup, availability projection, and uniform safe not-found handling in `apps/api/src/machines/application/resolve-machine-identifier.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- resolve-machine-identifier.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T067 [US2] Add explicit discriminated QR/manual resolve DTO validation in `apps/api/src/machines/http/dto/resolve-machine-identifier.dto.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api build`\n+- [ ] T068 [US2] Add the thin authenticated `POST /v1/machines/resolve` action to `apps/api/src/machines/http/machine-discovery.controller.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- resolve-machine.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T069 [US2] Implement camera-only permission normalization, supported-code scanning, focus/background preview shutdown, and idempotent disposal in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/native/ExpoScannerAdapter.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- ExpoScannerAdapter.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T070 [US2] Extend `MachineDiscoveryFlowService` with generation-guarded QR/manual `switchMap`, duplicate scan suppression, and scanner transitions in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.resolve.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T071 [US2] Visually inspect `docs/design/mockups/10_qr_scanner_hd.png` and append scanner hierarchy, safe-area, overlay, manual fallback, keyboard, permission, and focus observations to `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`, excluding all illustrative codes and business data; validate by rereading `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`\n+- [ ] T072 [P] [US2] Implement the controlled, keyboard-safe manual code form with validation/error/loading states and no independent business state in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/components/ManualMachineCodeForm.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck`\n+- [ ] T073 [US2] Add scanner screen tests for permission states, unavailable camera, focus-loss preview stop, repeated detections, invalid QR, safe not-found, manual fallback, keyboard avoidance, and success navigation in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineScannerScreen.spec.tsx`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineScannerScreen.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T074 [US2] Implement the observer-wrapped QR scanner/manual fallback screen with Safe Area and focus-driven preview lifecycle in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineScannerScreen.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineScannerScreen.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T075 [US2] Register the typed scanner route and discovery-to-scanner entry point in `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.tsx`, updating `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.spec.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MainNavigator.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T076 [US2] Add an independent fixture-backed scanner/manual journey covering valid versioned QR, arbitrary URL rejection, duplicate QR suppression, denied camera fallback, and uniform unknown-code handling in `apps/mobile/e2e/machine-identification.yaml`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec maestro test e2e/machine-identification.yaml`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US2 independently delivers safe exact machine identification through QR or manual input.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Inspect and Select an Available Machine (Priority: P1)\n+\n+**Goal**: A customer can inspect a freshly refreshed safe card and confirm only a current `ONLINE` machine, producing an ephemeral typed navigation handoff with no persistence or purchase side effect.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Open a deterministic machine directly by public ID, mutate price/publication/evidence through the test harness between card and confirmation, and verify detail refresh, context-changed/non-selectable responses, successful typed handoff, duplicate-tap suppression, and zero database writes beyond fixture control.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T077 [P] [US3] Add service tests for fresh gateway detail refresh, safe fallback name, exact current price, availability, opaque `machineRevision`, and uniform not-found behavior in `apps/api/src/machines/application/get-machine-detail.service.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- get-machine-detail.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T078 [P] [US3] Add selection tests for current price/publication/availability refresh, expected-revision comparison, `MACHINE_CONTEXT_CHANGED` with fresh safe card, `MACHINE_NOT_SELECTABLE`, `ONLINE`-only typed handoff, and no persistent side effects in `apps/api/src/machines/application/revalidate-machine-selection.service.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- revalidate-machine-selection.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T079 [P] [US3] Add authenticated Supertest/OpenAPI tests for `GET /v1/machines/{machineId}` and `POST /v1/machines/{machineId}/selection-revalidation`, including auth, ID/revision validation, detail refresh, price/status/publication changes, safe errors, public allowlist, and unchanged database row counts in `apps/api/test/machines/machine-selection.e2e-spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-selection.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T080 [P] [US3] Add mobile flow tests for detail `switchMap`, selection-confirmation `exhaustMap`, repeated tap suppression, context-changed card replacement, non-selectable recovery, generation checks, and typed handoff creation in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.selection.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.selection.spec.ts`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T081 [US3] Extend detail-by-public-ID and selection snapshot queries in `apps/api/src/machines/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-machine.repository.ts`, keeping aliases/evidence/internal UUIDs private; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- get-machine-detail.service.spec.ts revalidate-machine-selection.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T082 [US3] Implement fresh gateway evidence retrieval, projection, public detail revision calculation, and safe detail assembly in `apps/api/src/machines/application/get-machine-detail.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- get-machine-detail.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T083 [US3] Implement side-effect-free selection revalidation and typed handoff creation in `apps/api/src/machines/application/revalidate-machine-selection.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- revalidate-machine-selection.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T084 [US3] Add explicit machine path/revision DTO validation in `apps/api/src/machines/http/dto/machine-id-param.dto.ts` and `apps/api/src/machines/http/dto/revalidate-machine-selection.dto.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api build`\n+- [ ] T085 [US3] Implement thin authenticated detail and selection-revalidation actions in `apps/api/src/machines/http/machine-selection.controller.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-selection.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T086 [US3] Extend the mobile API adapter with fresh detail and selection-revalidation calls plus context-changed decoding in `apps/mobile/src/api/machine-discovery-api.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-api.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T087 [US3] Extend `MachineDiscoveryFlowService` with detail `switchMap`, confirmation `exhaustMap`, revision-aware card replacement, non-selectable handling, and typed handoff transition in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.selection.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T088 [US3] Visually inspect `docs/design/mockups/04_machine_purchase_hd.png` and append only machine-card hierarchy, spacing, typography, status, price, and primary-confirmation observations to `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`, explicitly excluding volume, totals, purchase/payment, sample data, and unapproved machine imagery; validate by rereading `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`\n+- [ ] T089 [US3] Add detail screen tests for loading, service/offline/stale/error states, refreshed price/status, context-changed replacement, disabled confirmation, repeated taps, Safe Area, and typed handoff navigation in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDetailScreen.spec.tsx`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineDetailScreen.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T090 [US3] Implement the observer-wrapped machine detail/card and final selection confirmation UI without volume, totals, purchase, reservation, payment, or wallet behavior in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDetailScreen.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineDetailScreen.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T091 [US3] Register the typed machine-detail route and navigation-only selection handoff exactly as specified in `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.tsx` and `apps/mobile/src/navigation/machine-selection-handoff.ts`, updating `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.spec.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MainNavigator.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T092 [US3] Add an independent fixture/emulator journey for detail refresh, price change, service/offline transition, context-changed response, repeated confirmation taps, successful handoff, and absence of selection writes in `apps/mobile/e2e/machine-selection.yaml`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec maestro test e2e/machine-selection.yaml`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US3 independently delivers current detail inspection and safe, side-effect-free selection.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Receive Safe and Current Results (Priority: P2)\n+\n+**Goal**: Customers receive only current, allowlisted results; stale catalog contexts and delayed obsolete responses fail safely without corrupting visible state.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Mutate the catalog ordering revision and delay emulator/API responses while issuing newer requests; verify stale cursors are rejected, late results are ignored, public payloads remain allowlisted, and the UI presents refreshable stale/error states.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 4\n+\n+- [ ] T093 [P] [US4] Add integration tests for catalog ordering revision increments on ordering-relevant catalog changes and stale cursor rejection without duplicates/omissions in `apps/api/test/machines/machine-catalog-revision.integration-spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- machine-catalog-revision.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T094 [P] [US4] Add cross-route contract assertions that every success/context-changed/error payload matches `contracts/machine-discovery.openapi.yaml` and excludes sensitive/internal fields in `apps/api/test/machines/machine-public-boundary.e2e-spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-public-boundary.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T095 [P] [US4] Add mobile tests proving delayed stale discovery/detail/resolve/revalidation responses cannot mutate the current store after a newer request generation in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T096 [P] [US4] Add screen tests for stale catalog refresh, transport/offline recovery, stale evidence display as unavailable, retry supersession, and preservation of safe current data during refresh in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDiscoverySafetyStates.spec.tsx`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineDiscoverySafetyStates.spec.tsx`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 4\n+\n+- [ ] T097 [US4] Add transactionally maintained ordering-revision updates for publication, location, service-area, and ordering-key changes to `apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260813000100_add_machine_discovery_catalog/migration.sql` and expose revision reads in `apps/api/src/machines/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-machine.repository.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- machine-catalog-revision.integration-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T098 [US4] Map stale ordering revisions, expired/mismatched cursors, freshness failures, and all route errors through the same consumer-safe taxonomy in `apps/api/src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.ts` and `apps/api/src/machines/http/machine-error.filter.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-public-boundary.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T099 [US4] Enforce the public response DTO allowlist on all four controller actions in `apps/api/src/machines/http/machine-discovery.controller.ts` and `apps/api/src/machines/http/machine-selection.controller.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-public-boundary.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T100 [US4] Harden `MachineDiscoveryFlowService` reducers so only the active session epoch and request generation can commit, while stale/transport failures preserve or clear data according to typed state transitions in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T101 [US4] Implement reusable presentation-only loading, empty, denied, offline, service, stale, and consumer-safe error states in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/components/MachineDiscoveryState.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck`\n+- [ ] T102 [US4] Integrate refreshable safe-current-result states without duplicating MobX state across discovery/detail/scanner screens in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDiscoveryScreen.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDetailScreen.tsx`, and `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineScannerScreen.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineDiscoverySafetyStates.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T103 [US4] Add an independent delayed-response and stale-cursor fixture journey covering revision change, retry, freshness boundary, and public-field redaction in `apps/mobile/e2e/machine-safe-current-results.yaml`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec maestro test e2e/machine-safe-current-results.yaml`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US4 independently demonstrates stale-result rejection and consumer-safe outputs under catalog and network races.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 7: User Story 5 - Keep Machine Data Session-Safe (Priority: P2)\n+\n+**Goal**: Logout, account replacement, and disposal cancel active machine work and prevent any prior-session result or handoff from entering the next session.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Start delayed discovery/detail/QR/selection work, replace or clear the authenticated account before completion, and verify cancellation, epoch isolation, full state clearing, fresh composition scope, and idempotent disposal.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 5\n+\n+- [ ] T104 [P] [US5] Add flow tests for `takeUntil` cancellation on logout, account replacement, and disposal across discovery/detail/QR/manual/confirmation streams in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.session.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.session.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T105 [P] [US5] Add store tests for epoch increments and atomic clearing of discovery, catalog, permissions, scanner, card/detail, errors, generations, and handoff on session change in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/stores/machine-discovery.store.session.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery.store.session.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T106 [P] [US5] Add composition-root tests for account-keyed scope replacement, disposal of adapters/subscriptions, no long-lived public subjects, and repeated idempotent `dispose()` calls in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/machine-discovery-composition-root.spec.ts`; verify the new test fails with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-composition-root.spec.ts`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 5\n+\n+- [ ] T107 [US5] Implement atomic session-epoch replacement and complete feature-state clearing in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/stores/machine-discovery.store.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery.store.session.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T108 [US5] Add private cancellation subjects, `takeUntil` boundaries, epoch/generation tagging, late-result rejection, and idempotent subscription disposal in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-flow.session.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T109 [US5] Bind the feature lifetime to authenticated account identity and dispose the prior scope before constructing the next in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/machine-discovery-composition-root.ts` and `apps/mobile/src/App.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-composition-root.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T110 [US5] Add an independent delayed-response journey proving logout/account replacement clears machine state and blocks old-session catalog, card, scanner, error, and handoff results in `apps/mobile/e2e/machine-session-isolation.yaml`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec maestro test e2e/machine-session-isolation.yaml`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: US5 independently demonstrates account/session isolation under in-flight asynchronous work.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase 8: Polish and Cross-Cutting Validation\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate the complete contract, production gates, responsive visuals, security boundaries, and documented fixture workflows.\n+\n+- [ ] T111 [P] Add automated OpenAPI structure/response validation for all four authenticated routes against `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/contracts/machine-discovery.openapi.yaml` in `apps/api/test/machines/machine-discovery.openapi-spec.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- machine-discovery.openapi-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T112 [P] Add architecture tests preventing machine controllers from containing domain/query logic and preventing imports for ERP, MQTT commands, payment, wallet commands, reservation, purchase, or dispensing in `apps/api/src/machines/machine-boundaries.spec.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- machine-boundaries.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T113 [P] Add mobile architecture tests enforcing one MobX state owner, presentation-oriented screens, private RxJS subjects, explicit disposal, and API/SecureStore access only through typed adapters in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/machine-discovery-boundaries.spec.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- machine-discovery-boundaries.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T114 Add the complete controlled fixture/emulator scenario suite from `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/quickstart.md` to `apps/api/test/machines/machine-discovery-quickstart.e2e-spec.ts`, covering availability/freshness, coordinates/money/identifiers, pagination, resolve, detail refresh, selection races, safe errors, and no side effects; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test:e2e -- machine-discovery-quickstart.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T115 Add a production-startup gate test and implementation that refuse emulator, fixture seed, and legacy QR modes while requiring non-default cursor secrets in `apps/api/src/machines/machine-production-gates.spec.ts` and `apps/api/src/machines/machines.module.ts`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api test -- machine-production-gates.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T116 Verify Safe Area, keyboard avoidance, camera focus lifecycle, and compact/large iOS and Android layouts in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineResponsiveLayout.spec.tsx`, fixing only responsive defects in `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDiscoveryScreen.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineDetailScreen.tsx`, and `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineScannerScreen.tsx`; verify with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test -- MachineResponsiveLayout.spec.tsx`\n+- [ ] T117 Compare the implemented discovery, detail, and scanner screens with `docs/design/mockups/03_machine_selection_hd.png`, `docs/design/mockups/04_machine_purchase_hd.png`, and `docs/design/mockups/10_qr_scanner_hd.png`, recording and resolving material visual differences without copying demo business data in `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`; verify with updated iOS and Android screenshots referenced from `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/ui-notes.md`\n+- [ ] T118 Run backend schema generation, build, targeted unit/integration/e2e suites, and migration deployment against an empty test database, recording commands and results in `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/validation.md`; validate with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api prisma generate`, `pnpm --filter @kaynann/api build`, and the machine test suites listed in that file\n+- [ ] T119 Run mobile typecheck, unit/component suites, Expo dependency check, and all five Maestro journeys, recording commands and results in `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/validation.md`; validate with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck`, `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test`, and `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo install --check`\n+- [ ] T120 Update `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/quickstart.md` with the verified seed, emulator controls, test commands, production prohibitions, foreground-location/camera permissions, Maps secret injection, and explicit legacy-QR rollout gate; validate every documented command against `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/validation.md`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Phase Dependencies\n+\n+- **Phase 1 - Setup**: Starts immediately. T002 and T004 may run in parallel after T001 is not required; T003 depends on T002, T005 depends on T004, and T006 depends on T003 and T005.\n+- **Phase 2 - Foundational**: Depends on Phase 1. Database chain: T007 -> T008 -> T009 -> T010 -> T011 -> T012. Domain chains: T015 -> T016, T017 -> T018, T019 -> T020, T021 -> T022, T023 -> T024, and T025 -> T026. Infrastructure chain: T027 -> T028 -> T029 -> T030 -> T031 -> T032 -> T033. Mobile chain: T034 -> T035, T036 -> T037, T038 -> T039 -> T040.\n+- **Phases 3-7 - User Stories**: Each starts after Phase 2 and is independently testable. Priority execution is US1/US2/US3 (P1) before US4/US5 (P2), but separate teams may execute stories concurrently.\n+- **Phase 8 - Polish**: Depends on every story selected for release; T117 depends on all UI tasks, T118 depends on backend tasks, T119 depends on mobile tasks, and T120 depends on T118-T119.\n+\n+## User Story Dependencies\n+\n+- **US1 (P1)**: Depends only on Foundational. It owns catalog discovery and map/list presentation.\n+- **US2 (P1)**: Depends only on Foundational. It resolves fixtures directly and does not require US1 discovery.\n+- **US3 (P1)**: Depends only on Foundational. Its independent test opens a fixture by known public `machineId`; navigation integration may reuse US1/US2 entry points after both exist.\n+- **US4 (P2)**: Depends only on Foundational for its independent delayed/stale harness. For release hardening, apply it after US1-US3 so all four routes and three screens receive the protections.\n+- **US5 (P2)**: Depends only on Foundational and mocked flows for independent session-isolation testing. For release, apply it after active US1-US3 workflows exist.\n+\n+## Within-Story Dependencies\n+\n+- **US1**: T041-T046 are written and observed failing first; T047 depends on T041-T042; T048 depends on T043 and T047; T049-T050 depend on T048; T051 depends on T045; T052 depends on T037; T053 depends on T046 and T035; T054 precedes UI; T055-T056 depend on T054; T057 precedes T058; T059 follows T058; T060 follows the complete story.\n+- **US2**: T061-T064 fail first; T065-T066 satisfy T061; T067-T068 satisfy T062; T069 satisfies T063; T070 satisfies T064; T071 precedes UI; T072 and T073 precede T074; T075 follows T074; T076 follows the complete story.\n+- **US3**: T077-T080 fail first; T081 precedes T082-T083; T084-T085 follow services; T086-T087 satisfy the mobile flow test; T088 precedes UI; T089 precedes T090; T091 follows handoff implementation; T092 follows the complete story.\n+- **US4**: T093-T096 fail first; T097-T099 satisfy backend safety tests; T100 satisfies delayed-response tests; T101 precedes T102; T103 follows the complete story.\n+- **US5**: T104-T106 fail first; T107 satisfies store clearing; T108 depends on T107; T109 depends on T108; T110 follows the complete story.\n+\n+## Parallel Opportunities\n+\n+- Setup test tasks T002 and T004 affect different applications and can run in parallel.\n+- After T012, foundational domain test/implementation chains T015-T026 can be split by file; mobile chains T034-T040 can proceed alongside backend infrastructure T027-T033.\n+- After Foundational, US1-US5 can start in parallel because each has fixture/fake-backed independent tests; integrate shared files such as `machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`, controllers, repository, and navigator sequentially in Task ID order to avoid conflicts.\n+- Within stories, only tasks carrying `[P]` are safe concurrent edits. Tasks sharing `apps/api/src/machines/infrastructure/postgres/prisma-machine.repository.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.service.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/navigation/MainNavigator.tsx`, or the same screen are deliberately not marked `[P]`.\n+- Polish architecture/OpenAPI tests T111-T113 can run concurrently; final validation/documentation T118-T120 remains ordered.\n+\n+## Parallel Execution Examples\n+\n+### User Story 1\n+\n+```text\n+Parallel batch A: T041, T042, T043, T044, T045, T046\n+After backend tests exist: T047 -> T048 -> T049 -> T050\n+After mockup notes T054: T055 and T056 in parallel, then T057 -> T058 -> T059 -> T060\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 2\n+\n+```text\n+Parallel batch A: T061, T062, T063, T064\n+Backend chain: T065 -> T066 -> T067 -> T068\n+Mobile chain: T069 -> T070; after T071, T072 can proceed while T073 is written, then T074 -> T075 -> T076\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 3\n+\n+```text\n+Parallel batch A: T077, T078, T079, T080\n+Backend chain: T081 -> T082 and T083 -> T084 -> T085\n+Mobile chain: T086 -> T087; after T088, T089 -> T090 -> T091 -> T092\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 4\n+\n+```text\n+Parallel batch A: T093, T094, T095, T096\n+Backend chain: T097 -> T098 -> T099\n+Mobile chain: T100 -> T101 -> T102, then T103\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 5\n+\n+```text\n+Parallel batch A: T104, T105, T106\n+Implementation chain: T107 -> T108 -> T109 -> T110\n+```\n+\n+## Implementation Strategy\n+\n+1. Complete Setup and Foundational in dependency order; do not expose a route or screen before database/domain/public-boundary invariants are executable.\n+2. Implement each story test-first: add the listed failing tests, confirm the expected failure, make the smallest implementation diff, and run only the targeted command before moving on.\n+3. Deliver the three P1 stories in order for a single-team path: discovery, exact identification, then fresh detail/selection. Each remains fixture/emulator-backed and independently demonstrable.\n+4. Add P2 stale-result and session-safety hardening, then run cross-cutting contract, architecture, production-gate, responsive, visual, and end-to-end validation.\n+5. Keep the production machine protocol boundary fail-closed. Development and tests use only the standalone emulator and deterministic application-owned fixtures; production emulator/fixture/legacy-QR modes remain forbidden or disabled until separately verified inputs exist.\n+\n+## MVP Scope\n+\n+The minimum complete machine-selection flow is **Phase 1 Setup + Phase 2 Foundational + US1 + US2 + US3**. Discovery alone is not a usable MVP: the customer must be able to find candidates, identify the exact physical machine, inspect refreshed price/status, and confirm a current `ONLINE` machine into the typed navigation handoff. US4 and US5 are P2 hardening increments required before a production-ready release but are not prerequisites for demonstrating the controlled MVP flow.\n*** End Patch";
