2026-08-13T17:04:58.017885Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019ffbdd-c8a4-7d61-9468-1b9c7ea99658}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019ffc14-7d51-74e1-befd-8d400172e515" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019ffbdd-c8a4-7d61-9468-1b9c7ea99658 turn.id=019ffc14-7d51-74e1-befd-8d400172e515 model=gpt-5.6-sol codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/spec.md\n@@\n-- A published machine without valid coordinates is excluded from map markers and nearest-distance ordering; it may only be resolved through another supported path if its required card and eligibility data remain valid.\n+- A published machine without valid coordinates is excluded from map markers and all discovery-list results; it may only be resolved through QR or manual exact identification if its required card and eligibility data remain valid.\n@@\n-- **FR-026**: A newer accepted position, viewed area, search context, session, or refresh MUST supersede older in-progress work, and older results MUST NOT replace newer visible state.\n+- **FR-026**: A newer accepted position, viewport, service area, session, or refresh MUST supersede older in-progress work, and older results MUST NOT replace newer visible state.\n@@\n-- **MachineLocation**: The customer-visible address and geographic coordinates associated with a machine, including the currency context needed to present its price. Multiple machines may share the same address while remaining individually identifiable.\n+- **MachineLocation**: The customer-visible address, explicit service-area assignment, and geographic coordinates associated with a machine. Multiple machines may share the same address while remaining individually identifiable; currency belongs only to `MachinePrice` and is never inferred from location.\n@@\n ### Measurable Outcomes\n+\n+Unless a criterion explicitly says otherwise, timed acceptance uses a warm authenticated application, the deterministic fixture catalog, a supported release device, and a controlled network profile with 100 ms round-trip latency, at most 20 ms jitter, and zero injected packet loss. Automated latency criteria use at least 100 measured runs and pass when at least 95 runs meet the stated threshold. Physical QR and interaction acceptance uses at least 20 recorded trials on each supported platform and passes when at least 19 trials meet the stated threshold.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/plan.md\n@@\n-- The opaque signed keyset cursor binds the normalized query context, catalog\n+- The opaque signed keyset cursor binds the normalized query context, catalog\n@@\n-- Optional viewport bounds are validated, bounded, and cursor-bound. Invalid or\n-  missing machine coordinates are excluded from map/distance results but may be\n-  shown in list results without distance when their public address and explicit\n-  application-owned service-area assignment are valid.\n+- Optional viewport bounds are validated, bounded, and cursor-bound. Invalid or\n+  missing machine coordinates are excluded from map markers and discovery-list\n+  results. They remain reachable only through exact QR or manual identification\n+  when their public card and eligibility data are otherwise valid.\n - User coordinates are request-scoped only and are not persisted or included in\n   application logs/analytics.\n+\n+### Acceptance performance profile\n+\n+- Timed acceptance uses a warm authenticated application, deterministic fixtures,\n+  a supported release device, and a controlled network with 100 ms round-trip\n+  latency, at most 20 ms jitter, and no injected packet loss.\n+- Discovery and selection latency use at least 100 automated measured runs and\n+  require at least 95% of runs to meet their specification thresholds.\n+- QR timing and the three-interaction card-opening outcome use at least 20 recorded\n+  trials per supported platform and require at least 19 successful trials.\n+- Performance validation records the device/runtime, fixture size, network profile,\n+  raw timings, percentile calculation, failures, and exact commands or protocol.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/data-model.md\n@@\n-- Missing/invalid coordinates exclude a machine from map markers and distance\n-  ranking. A published machine with a valid address and configured\n-  `serviceAreaCode` may remain in unlocated list discovery with no\n-  `distanceMeters` field.\n+- Missing/invalid coordinates exclude a machine from map markers and all\n+  discovery-list results. Such a machine may still resolve through exact QR or\n+  manual identification when its public card and eligibility data are valid.\n*** End Patch";
text(await tools.apply_patch(patch));
