And Unit Suites\n+\n+```bash\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck\n+# PASS\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec vitest run \\\n+  src/machine-discovery/screens/MachineResponsiveLayout.spec.tsx \\\n+  src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts\n+# PASS: 2 files, 19 tests\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec vitest run \\\n+  src/machine-discovery/testing/machine-discovery-e2e-bootstrap.spec.ts \\\n+  src/machine-discovery/machine-discovery-boundaries.spec.ts\n+# PASS: 2 files, 17 tests\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test\n+# PASS: 53 files, 323 tests\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo install --check\n+# PASS: dependencies match the installed Expo SDK\n+```\n+\n+The Expo dependency check ran without registry access and used Expo's local\n+`bundledNativeModules.json` metadata. The first complete mobile test run caught\n+a direct `fetch` implementation in the machine-discovery testing layer. The\n+typed E2E control HTTP adapter was moved to `apps/mobile/src/api/`, leaving the\n+testing bootstrap as an injected consumer; the boundary tests and complete\n+suite then passed.\n+\n+## Runtime Build And API Contract\n+\n+The test-only API host started successfully against the disposable database,\n+and the fixture bootstrap returned the expected environment marker, catalog,\n+account, acceptance time, API origin, and fixture credential provenance. An\n+exact E2E Android build selected and bundled `apps/mobile/index.e2e.ts`:\n+\n+```bash\n+EAS_BUILD_PROFILE=machine-discovery-e2e APP_ENV=e2e \\\n+  EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=e2e \\\n+  EXPO_PUBLIC_BUILD_VARIANT=machine-discovery-e2e \\\n+  EXPO_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_DISTRIBUTABLE=false \\\n+  pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo run:android --variant release\n+# PASS: x86_64 APK built and installed\n+```\n+\n+The first discovery launch exposed a public contract defect: PostGIS returned a\n+fractional distance while the OpenAPI contract and strict mobile decoder require\n+an integer `distanceMeters`. The public projection now rounds distance while\n+the exact repository distance remains in the signed pagination cursor.\n+\n+```bash\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api exec vitest run \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.spec.ts\n+# PASS: 1 file, 10 tests\n+\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api exec eslint \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.ts \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.spec.ts\n+# PASS\n+\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api build\n+# PASS\n+```\n+\n+After that fix, the running E2E client rendered both deterministic machine cards\n+with integer distances. No schema, migration, authentication, or persisted\n+selection behavior changed.\n+\n+## Maestro Runtime Results\n+\n+All five files were invoked individually against the isolated build so one\n+failure would not hide the status of the other journeys:\n+\n+```bash\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/machine-discovery.yaml\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/machine-identification.yaml\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/machine-selection.yaml\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/machine-safe-current-results.yaml\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/machine-session-isolation.yaml\n+# INCOMPLETE: 0 of 5 journeys completed\n+```\n+\n+- `machine-discovery.yaml` loaded both fixture machines and rendered their list\n+  cards, but failed the first `machine-marker-*` assertion. Android Maps first\n+  crashed when no deployment key was injected. A transient placeholder value\n+  allowed the native view to initialize, but Google rejected it, leaving the\n+  map surface and markers unavailable. A valid `GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY`\n+  must be supplied externally; the placeholder is not acceptance evidence.\n+- The other four journeys reached the application title, then failed their\n+  first scanner/card assertion because an Android location permission dialog\n+  still covered the UI. On Android 37.1, Maestro 2.10.0's launch-time\n+  `location: deny` reset the permission to undetermined rather than confirming\n+  the user denial. The captured hierarchies contain the system\n+  `permission_deny_button`, not the asserted application element.\n+- Completion requires a supported Android runtime/tool pairing that can set a\n+  deterministic denied state, or explicit cross-platform system-dialog handling\n+  in the authored journeys, plus a valid externally injected Android Maps key.\n+  App-level permission or map bypasses must not be added merely to make E2E pass.\n+\n+The production selector was restored after the attempt:\n+\n+```bash\n+APP_ENV=production EAS_BUILD_PROFILE=production \\\n+  node apps/mobile/scripts/select-machine-discovery-entry.cjs\n+# PASS: apps/mobile/package.json main is index.ts\n+```\n+\n+The test-only API and Metro processes were stopped, the emulator was shut down,\n+and querying PostgreSQL after cleanup returned zero databases named\n+`kaynann_t119_validation_20260901`.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/tasks.md\n@@\n - [ ] T119 After T124, run mobile typecheck, unit/component suites, Expo dependency check, and the runtime execution of all five previously authored Maestro journeys, recording commands and results in `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/validation.md`; validate with `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck`, `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test`, `pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo install --check`, and `maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/`\n+  - Validation attempt 2026-09-01: static/unit checks passed, but runtime remains incomplete because Android Maps had no valid externally injected key and Maestro 2.10.0 on Android 37.1 left `location: deny` at the system prompt; see `validation.md`. Keep T119 unchecked until all five journeys pass.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-machine/.codex/docs/session-handoff.md\n@@\n ## Current State\n@@\n - Mobile native launch arguments are autolinked only for the exact\n   non-distributable E2E build profile. Production mobile and API build graphs do\n   not import the E2E entry, native module, bootstrap, host, or routes.\n+- T119 static validation is now green: mobile typecheck, 53-file/323-test suite,\n+  targeted bootstrap/boundary tests, Expo dependency check, and the isolated\n+  Android E2E build all passed.\n+- The runtime attempt found and fixed a real response-contract defect: public\n+  `distanceMeters` is now rounded to an integer while the exact distance remains\n+  in the pagination cursor. Its targeted 10-test suite, ESLint, and API build\n+  pass.\n+- All five Maestro files were invoked, but none completed on the available\n+  Android 37.1 emulator. Discovery requires a valid externally injected Google\n+  Maps Android key; the other four flows are covered by an undismissed system\n+  location prompt because Maestro 2.10.0 leaves `location: deny` undetermined on\n+  this runtime. T119 therefore remains unchecked and the count remains 123/131.\n+- The disposable T119 database was dropped, runtime processes and emulator were\n+  stopped, and `apps/mobile/package.json` was restored to `main: index.ts`.\n@@\n ## Next Single Diff\n \n - Complete only `T119`; do not start performance, legacy QR, or release\n   documentation tasks.\n-- Resolve the eight existing mobile test-only type errors, then run the complete\n-  mobile typecheck, unit/component suite, and Expo dependency check.\n-- Start the test-only API host and a non-distributable E2E mobile build with the\n-  exact fixture origin/control variables, then execute all five authored\n-  Maestro journeys.\n-- Record commands, environment prerequisites, and results in\n-  `specs/006-machine-discovery-and-selection/validation.md`; update `tasks.md`\n-  and this handoff only when T119 is genuinely complete, then stop.\n+- Supply a valid `GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY` only through the local/deployment\n+  environment; never persist or print it. Rebuild the exact non-distributable\n+  `machine-discovery-e2e` Android entry against the fixture API.\n+- Make denied location/camera setup deterministic by using a supported\n+  Android/Maestro pairing or by adding explicit cross-platform handling for the\n+  native permission dialog to the authored journeys. Do not add an app-level\n+  map or permission bypass solely for E2E.\n+- Execute `maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/` and require all five journeys to pass.\n+  Then mark T119 complete, update validation and this handoff, restore\n+  `main: index.ts`, clean the disposable runtime, and stop.\n@@\n ## Latest Relevant Validation\n \n ```bash\n-pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec vitest run src/machine-discovery/testing/machine-discovery-e2e-bootstrap.spec.ts\n-# passed: 1 file, 12 tests\n-\n-pnpm --filter @kaynann/api exec vitest run test/machines/support/machine-discovery-e2e-control.spec.ts\n-# passed: 1 file, 10 tests\n-\n-pnpm exec eslint --max-warnings=0 <T124 mobile source and test files>\n-# passed\n-\n-pnpm exec eslint --max-warnings=0 <T124 API source and test files>\n-# passed\n-\n-EAS_BUILD_PROFILE=machine-discovery-e2e APP_ENV=e2e \\\n-  EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=e2e \\\n-  EXPO_PUBLIC_BUILD_VARIANT=machine-discovery-e2e \\\n-  EXPO_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_DISTRIBUTABLE=false \\\n-  node apps/mobile/scripts/select-machine-discovery-entry.cjs\n-# passed under the apps/mobile Node 12.18 runtime: main selected index.e2e.ts\n-\n-pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo export --platform android \\\n-  --output-dir /private/tmp/knn-t124-e2e-hook-export-3\n-# passed: Metro bundled apps/mobile/index.e2e.ts, 1159 modules\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck\n+# passed\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile test\n+# passed: 53 files, 323 tests\n+\n+pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile exec expo install --check\n+# passed using local Expo SDK metadata; network was unavailable\n+\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api exec vitest run \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.spec.ts\n+# passed: 1 file, 10 tests\n+\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api exec eslint \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.ts \\\n+  src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.spec.ts\n+# passed\n+\n+CI=true pnpm --filter @kaynann/api build\n+# passed\n+\n+maestro test apps/mobile/e2e/<each of the five authored files>\n+# incomplete: 0/5 completed; Maps key and Android permission-state blockers\n \n APP_ENV=production EAS_BUILD_PROFILE=production \\\n   node apps/mobile/scripts/select-machine-discovery-entry.cjs\n-# passed: apps/mobile/package.json main restored to index.ts\n-\n-APP_ENV=e2e node apps/mobile/scripts/select-machine-discovery-entry.cjs\n-# expected rejection: exact non-distributable EAS profile is required\n-\n-pnpm --filter @kaynann/mobile typecheck\n-# non-zero only for 8 existing test-only errors in\n-# MachineResponsiveLayout.spec.tsx and\n-# machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts\n-\n-pnpm --filter @kaynann/api typecheck\n-# non-zero only for 15 existing errors in prior machine test files; no T124 errors\n+# passed: apps/mobile/package.json main is index.ts\n ```\n@@\n ## Validation Still Needed\n \n-- T119 must make the complete mobile typecheck green and run the full mobile\n-  unit/component suite plus `expo install --check`.\n-- T119 must execute all five Maestro journeys against the runnable E2E mobile\n-  build and fixture API/PostgreSQL environment and record the results.\n+- T119 must complete all five Maestro journeys against the runnable E2E mobile\n+  build and fixture API/PostgreSQL environment. Static/unit validation is\n+  already green.\n - The E2E runtime requires explicit fixture-only values for the API origin,\n   allowed origins, and control credential; do not persist credentials in source\n   or `eas.json`.\n+- Android map execution additionally requires a valid deployment-secret Maps\n+  key injected outside source control. The placeholder used only to diagnose\n+  native initialization is invalid and is not acceptance evidence.\n+- Denied location/camera states must be deterministic on the chosen runtime;\n+  the Android 37.1/Maestro 2.10.0 combination used in this attempt did not apply\n+  a confirmed denial through `launchApp.permissions`.\n@@\n - `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/services/machine-discovery-flow.stale-results.spec.ts`\n+- `apps/mobile/src/api/machine-discovery-e2e-control-api.ts`\n+- `apps/mobile/src/machine-discovery/testing/machine-discovery-e2e-bootstrap.ts`\n - `apps/mobile/e2e/`\n+- `apps/api/src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.ts`\n+- `apps/api/src/machines/application/discover-machines.service.spec.ts`\n*** End Patch";
